    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Read the program given to you. Ask AI Tutor to explain parts you aren’t sure about.\r\n- Complete the `learn` function. It should add tokens and their followers to `model`. Specifically:\r\n  - The keys of `model` should be individual tokens.\r\n  - Each key’s value should be a list of tokens that could come right after it.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember that, to iterate over pairs of tokens, you can use a `for` loop, similar to how you did in the previous lesson.\r\n\r\n```\r\nfor i in range(len(tokens) - 1):\r\n  token = tokens[i]\r\n  follower = tokens[i + 1]\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf a token is already a key in `model`, you’ll want to add to its followers list. If a token isn’t already a key, you’ll want to start a new list. To check, use a conditional.\r\n\r\n```\r\nif token in model:\r\n  # Add to an existing list\r\nelse:\r\n  # Start a new list\r\n```",
